    Cache the Maven wrapper in CI (#8305)
    
    The Maven wrapper jar and the Maven distribution it downloads live
    outside of the cached local repository, so every CI run downloaded them
    again. If downloading the jar fails, mvnw stays silent and Maven fails
    with a confusing ClassNotFoundException for MavenWrapperMain.
    
    Both are now cached, keyed by the hash of mvnw and the wrapper
    properties. Updating the wrapper or Maven changes the key and thereby
    invalidates the cache. There are deliberately no restore keys, since
    mvnw only checks whether the jar exists and would silently keep using an
    outdated one.
    
